// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 08-alias-validity
// facility: rule.value-object.write [Write-Conflict]; inv.alias-validity
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// Regression for a real soundness bug: dereferencing a reference once
// used to record its token as an "ancestor" of the place it reached,
// permanently, so every later access to that place by anyone skipped
// it in the clash check. After `*r` had been read, the owner could
// write `x` while `r` was still live and held, and `r` then observed
// the mutation. The ancestor chain must belong to the one access that
// followed the reference, never to the place.

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto r = &x;
    i32 before = *r;
    x = 2;
    i32 after = *r;
}
